Input: {"question": "What is \"I Love New York\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 0, "end": 53, "text": "text at the bottom encouraged people to \"Be generous."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 54, "end": 74, "text": "Your city needs you."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 75, "end": 104, "text": "This poster is not for sale.\""}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 105, "end": 208, "text": "\"I Love New York\" was written and composed by Steve Karmen in 1977 as part of the advertising campaign."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 209, "end": 277, "text": "In 1980, Governor Hugh Carey declared it as New York's state anthem."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 278, "end": 441, "text": "In a move that was remarkable for Karmen, who is well known for retaining the publishing rights to his songs, he gave the rights to the song to the state for free."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 442, "end": 532, "text": "The logo has become a pop-culture icon, inspiring imitations in every corner of the globe."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d00", "start": 533, "end": 559, "text": "Merchandise proclaiming \"I"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d01", "start": 0, "end": 213, "text": "\"New York Goes to Hollywood\".) In addition to Pollard, a host of other individuals from \"Flavor of Love\", including \"Sister\" Patterson (Pollard's mother), appeared on the show to help Pollard choose the right man."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d01", "start": 214, "end": 293, "text": "Mauricio Sanchez played New York's assistant, \"Chamo,\" during the first season."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d01", "start": 294, "end": 433, "text": "The production of a second season of \"I Love New York\" was first announced during a commercial break for the April 29, 2007, episode of \"\"."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d01", "start": 434, "end": 558, "text": "After the show was wrapped up for season one, the house was used for another VH1 show, \"Flavor of Love Girls: Charm School\"."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d01", "start": 559, "end": 593, "text": "A large number of contestants from"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 0, "end": 30, "text": "her character with conviction."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 31, "end": 202, "text": "\"Filmfare\" reviewer Rachit Gupta gave the film 3 out of 5 stars criticising the film's \"mish-mash of sentimentality, annoying characters and clichéd rom com developments\"."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 203, "end": 326, "text": "Gupta also felt that Deol and Ranaut as a pair was a miscast, with Deol particularly not gelling as a romantic comedy lead."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 327, "end": 371, "text": "He also felt that the music was forgettable."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 372, "end": 506, "text": "However Gupta did praise Ranaut who he commented was the highlight of the film as \"She's quite literally too good to be in this film\"."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 507, "end": 583, "text": "The film collected nett in its entire theatrical run against the budget of ."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0433-e1103d5dac41:d02", "start": 584, "end": 587, "text": "The"}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["state anthem", "advertising campaign", "pop-culture icon", "logo"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "state anthem", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "advertising campaign", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "pop-culture icon", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "logo", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}

